From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:28:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bifrost): opt-in static inbound address filter

Operators can list addresses under bifrost.address_filter (default off). The
observer drops inbound observations whose sender is listed before they are
signed or gossiped; outbound observations of our own vaults are untouched.

The chain is inferred only from unambiguous, validated shapes: 0x + 40 hex
(all EVM chains), BTC bc1 (valid mainnet bech32/bech32m) and BTC legacy
(valid base58check with the mainnet P2PKH/P2SH version byte). Every other
chain needs an explicit CHAIN:address entry. Unprefixed entries of any other
shape, and bc1/legacy entries that fail checksum, are skipped and counted,
never guessed onto a chain and never fatal. Dropped inbounds are counted per
chain.
